  "articleBody": "Many personal injury lawyers hear 'AEO' and wonder if it's just a new buzzword for SEO. While both aim to improve online visibility, AEO, or Answer Engine Optimization, focuses specifically on how AI systems and conversational search engines find, interpret, and cite your content. Traditional SEO often targets keywords for a specific search results page, but AEO makes your information clear and digestible so systems like Google AI Overviews, Siri, or Alexa can directly answer questions using your firm as a source. It's about optimizing for the *answer*, not just the rank.\n\n**Key Differences**\nSEO primarily focuses on ranking for a handful of keywords within a single domain, aiming for the 10 blue links. AEO, on the other hand, optimizes for AI-cited answers across a multitude of conversational queries, ensuring your firm's expertise is surfaced when prospects ask specific questions. While SEO might add some schema to an existing CMS, AEO generates hundreds of dedicated, schema-dense static HTML pages, explicitly engineered for AI ingestion. Furthermore, AEO distributes this content across highly trusted platforms like GitHub, giving your information a 'clean data' bias and inherited domain trust, something traditional SEO doesn't typically address. We also start research from actual unanswered questions from Google Search Console, not just keyword tools, targeting what people *really* want to know.\n\nCurious if AEO is the right next step for your personal injury law firm? Let's discuss how your firm can become the trusted answer in AI search.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-30"
}